Font Licenses — hermes-canvas
==============================

All font files in this directory are licensed under the SIL Open Font License,
Version 1.1 (OFL). The OFL permits embedding (including @font-face self-hosting),
redistribution, and use in this public repository. No CDN is used at runtime;
the files below are self-hosted and the app stays offline/local.

Bundled fonts (from Google Fonts, latin subset, woff2):

  Inter-Variable.woff2
    Family: Inter
    Author: rsms (Rasmus Andersson)
    Source: https://github.com/rsms/inter
    License: OFL 1.1 (see OFL.txt)

  Oswald-Variable.woff2
    Family: Oswald
    Author: Vernon Adams
    Source: https://github.com/googlefonts/Oswald
    License: OFL 1.1 (see OFL.txt)
    Role: condensed display / uppercase brand chrome (replaces the former
    commercial condensed face).

  DMSerifDisplay-Regular.woff2
    Family: DM Serif Display
    Author: Colophon Foundry (Jonny Pinhorn)
    Source: https://github.com/googlefonts/dm-font
    License: OFL 1.1 (see OFL.txt)
    Role: serif/display title and wordmark face.

  CourierPrime-Regular.woff2, CourierPrime-Bold.woff2
    Family: Courier Prime
    Author: Alan Dye / Quote-Unquote
    Source: https://github.com/googlefonts/Courier-Prime
    License: OFL 1.1 (see OFL.txt)
    Role: monospace (matches the --h-font-mono stack).

Why these fonts?
----------------
The previously bundled faces are commercial fonts. Their foundry EULAs
prohibit distributing or uploading the font binaries to a public repository
(Blaze Type EULA: "sell, rent, sublicense, copy or distribute ... to any Third
Party"; "shall not allow Third Parties to access the Product ... by offering
it for download"; Pangram Pangram EULA §3.7 (commercial) / §2.6 (free):
"Distributing copies ... Uploading or downloading the Fonts on the internet
or making it available publicly"). They were removed. See git history for
the removal commit message, which names the deleted files.

The four OFL families above preserve the design roles:
  --h-font          -> Inter (body/UI)
  --h-font-display  -> Oswald (condensed uppercase chrome)
  --h-font-title    -> DM Serif Display (titles)
  --h-font-mono     -> Courier Prime (mono)

The full OFL 1.1 text follows. Copyright and author notices are preserved in
the font binaries' name tables.
